Insula: licences by directory
=============================

Insula is a fork of the core of the BrainVISA neuroimaging suite, developed at
CEA / NeuroSpin (formerly Institut Fédératif de Recherche 49) and by the
BrainVISA and Populse communities. The copyright in the imported code belongs
to its authors and to the CEA, CNRS and INRIA as stated in each file header;
the full history, with authorship, is preserved in this repository. Nothing
here removes or replaces any notice. SPDX identifiers follow the SPDX list.

Each directory below was imported unchanged from the upstream repository named
on its line, at the commit shown in docs/PLAN.md, plus the Fedora fix commits
listed there. The licence texts are in LICENSES/.

Directory           Licence              Upstream
------------------  -------------------  -----------------------------------
soma-base/          CECILL-B             github.com/populse/soma-base
soma-io/            CECILL-B             github.com/brainvisa/soma-io
aims-free/          CECILL-B             github.com/brainvisa/aims-free
aims-gpl/           CECILL-2.1           github.com/brainvisa/aims-gpl
anatomist-free/     CECILL-B             github.com/brainvisa/anatomist-free
anatomist-gpl/      CECILL-2.0           github.com/brainvisa/anatomist-gpl
brainvisa-cmake/    CECILL-B             github.com/brainvisa/brainvisa-cmake
brainvisa-share/    CECILL-B             github.com/brainvisa/brainvisa-share

CECILL-B is permissive (BSD-like). CECILL-2.0 and CECILL-2.1 are copyleft and
GPL-compatible; programs that link aims-gpl or anatomist-gpl are therefore
distributed under their terms.

